{"name":"Orangina","hex":"#fec615","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Orangina","blocks":[{"text":"Orangina is a French lightly carbonated beverage made from carbonated water, 12% citrus juice, as well as 2% orange pulp. Orangina is sweetened with sugar or high fructose corn syrup (glucose-fructose) and, in some markets, with artificial sweetener. Natural flavours are also added."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Orangina.jpg/330px-Orangina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orangina","wikidata":"Q605830"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/BLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG/500px-BLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/BLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG/1280px-BLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/BLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG/500px-BLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blood Orangina bottle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABLOOD_ORANGINA.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Orangina%2C_NYC_-_June_2014_2.jpg/500px-Orangina%2C_NYC_-_June_2014_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Orangina%2C_NYC_-_June_2014_2.jpg/1280px-Orangina%2C_NYC_-_June_2014_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Orangina%2C_NYC_-_June_2014_2.jpg/500px-Orangina%2C_NYC_-_June_2014_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Classic glass bottle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w